<title>USA: GenCorp completes debt conversion.</title>
<headline>GenCorp completes debt conversion.</headline>
<text>
<p>FAIRLAWN, Ohio, June 24 (euter) - GenCorp said Tuesday its debenture holders converted essentially all the company's $115 million in eight percent convertible subordinated debentures due 2002 to about 7.2 million common shares.</p>
<p>GenCorp debt holders had until June 23 to convert the debentures, which the company called for redemption on May 23.</p>
<p>The conversion price for the debentures was $16.065 per share of common stock, GenCorp said. As a result of the redemption, GenCorp said its pro-forma debt dropped to $175 million and equity increased to $250 million as of May 31.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
</text>
